
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E G : Points
AB ⟂ AC [00]
AD ⟂ BC [01]
A,E,C are collinear [02]
∠EBA = ∠CBE [03]
G,B,E are collinear [04]
D,G,A are collinear [05]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
F : Points
F,B,C are collinear [06]
BC ⟂ FE [07]

 * Proof steps:
001. A,E,C are collinear [02] & F,B,C are collinear [06] & AD ⟂ BC [01] & AB ⟂ AC [00] & BC ⟂ FE [07] ⇒  ∠EAB = ∠BFE [08]
002. F,B,C are collinear [06] & ∠EBA = ∠CBE [03] ⇒  ∠EBA = ∠FBE [09]
003. ∠EAB = ∠BFE [08] & ∠EBA = ∠FBE [09] (Similar Triangles)⇒  ∠AEB = ∠BEF [10]
004. A,E,C are collinear [02] & G,B,E are collinear [04] & D,G,A are collinear [05] & ∠AEB = ∠BEF [10] & BC ⟂ FE [07] & AD ⟂ BC [01] ⇒  ∠AEG = ∠EGA [11]
005. ∠AEG = ∠EGA [11] ⇒  AE = AG
